  │    "S": null,
  │    "E": "RG",
  │    "W": "LB",
  │    "text": "Danzig smells of grain and river mud. The granaries run along the waterfront for half a mile — massive timber buildings, each with its own watchman, each with its own rats. The Teutonic Knights held this city until thirty years ago. Their influence did not leave when their garrison did. The grain factors still keep their books in German. The dock workers still cross themselves at the Knight chapel on the hill, out of habit or fear or both.\n\nA Hanseatic cog sits in the outer harbor with its hold open. It has been sitting there for four days. The harbormaster will not say why. The grain merchants will not say why. The captain drinks at the end of the pier and watches the water.",
