2026-05-30 01:48:50.102  POST    quest
  │  → body
  │  {
  │    "id": "quest_1367_a_najera",
  │    "type": "combat",
  │    "title": "The Free Company",
  │    "desc": "Seven Navarrese mercenaries block the road south of Nájera. They want tolls. Renaud le Bâtard has nothing left to pay.",
  │    "hint": "They outnumber you. They are tired and recently unpaid. That is an advantage.",
  │    "activateNode": "CY",
  │    "activateCond": "() => true",
  │    "xpAward": 150,
  │    "retryable": true,
  │    "retryGateDays": 0,
  │    "vignetteText": "The road out of Castile is rutted and smells of old smoke. Seven men across it. Not bandits — routiers, which is a different thing. Bandits want your gold. Routiers want your gold and also your acknowledgment that they could take everything else if they chose. The distinction matters. Routiers can be reasoned with, if you know the language.",
  │    "passText": "You put three of them down before the others decide the toll is not worth it. Not killed — the routier code frowns on unnecessary killing of fellow professionals. Wounded, winded, and reconsidering. The sergeant gives you a nod as you pass. Professional courtesy. The road is open.",
  │    "failText": "They take the toll. They are not unkind about it. One of them bandages your arm where the sword caught it. They have a fire going. They offer you some of it. You decline and walk south, lighter than you started.",
  │    "onPass": "() => { S_story.faction_hansa = Math.max(-5, (S_story.faction_hansa || 0) - 1); }",
  │    "onFail": "() => {}",
  │    "disposition": "The free companies did not end when the wars ended. The wars ended and the companies kept going. That is the problem with professional soldiers — they are very good at the one thing and the one thing keeps being needed."
  │  }
