2026-05-30 01:49:51.474  POST    quest
  │  → body
  │  {
  │    "id": "quest_1367_b_tamerlane",
  │    "type": "skill_check",
  │    "title": "The Warlord on the Eastern Wind",
  │    "desc": "A displaced scholar fleeing Transoxiana carries something important. Marta of Ragusa must spot the threat before it reaches him.",
  │    "hint": "The danger is not the scholar. It is whoever followed him west.",
  │    "activateNode": "CY",
  │    "activateCond": "() => true",
  │    "checkAbility": "wis",
  │    "checkLabel": "Perception",
  │    "checkDC": 13,
  │    "xpAward": 120,
  │    "retryable": true,
  │    "retryGateDays": 0,
  │    "vignetteText": "The scholar arrived three days ago from the east, thin, carrying a leather satchel he has not put down since he arrived. He says Tamerlane burned his library. He says this quietly, the way people state facts they have not yet finished believing. He is a fact-carrier. What concerns Marta is the two men who arrived one day after him and have been watching the caravan from the treeline.",
  │    "passText": "You see the watcher in the treeline shift position at dusk — the small movement of someone who has been still too long. You move first. The scholar gets out. The satchel goes with him. What is in it, you do not know. The scholar says only: it must reach the west. You believe him.",
  │    "failText": "The watcher moves at dawn, faster than you expected. The scholar is gone by midday — with the satchel, which is the important thing. But you do not know where he went, and the two men from the treeline are asking the caravan master questions you do not like the sound of.",
  │    "onPass": "() => { S_story.faith_folk = Math.min(5, (S_story.faith_folk || 0) + 1); }",
  │    "onFail": "() => {}",
  │    "disposition": "Tamerlane is not yet the destroyer of cities. In 1367 he is a warlord who reads books and burns them both. The scholars run west. Some of what they carry is worth the running."
  │  }
