  │      "text": "The river gate of Lübeck is where the Baltic begins and the old world ends. Every bale of wool, every barrel of herring, every block of amber that moves between England and Riga passes through this counting house or one exactly like it. The Hanseatic factor at the long table does not look up when you enter. He is adding numbers. The numbers are always right. That is the point.\n\nThe League does not fight wars. It embargoes. It withdraws its ships, closes its storehouses, and waits. Cities that lose Hansa trade do not burn — they simply run out of everything, quietly, over two seasons. The factor knows this. You are about to learn it.",
